<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 05:31:04 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>卢浮宫精选伊斯兰杰作首次来到美国。参观即将在史密森国家亚洲艺术博物馆展出的珍品</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-the-first-time-a-selection-of-islamic-masterpieces-from-the-louvre-is-coming-to-the-united-states-see-the-treasures-soon-to-be-displayed-at-the-smithsonians-national-museum-of-asian-art-180989402/</link><description>九月的展览将展出跨越多个世纪和地区的 26 件作品，题为“来自卢浮宫：伊斯兰艺术杰作”</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 19:00:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-the-first-time-a-selection-of-islamic-masterpieces-from-the-louvre-is-coming-to-the-united-states-see-the-treasures-soon-to-be-displayed-at-the-smithsonians-national-museum-of-asian-art-180989402/</guid></item><item><title>本周将目光转向夜空，观看近乎全食的月食。它会暂时把月亮变成红色</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/turn-your-eyes-to-the-night-skies-this-week-to-see-a-near-total-lunar-eclipse-itll-temporarily-turn-the-moon-red-180989404/</link><description>在高峰期，月球 96% 的面积将位于地球阴影最暗的部分内。由于阳光穿过地球大气层，该球体将呈现出怪异的光芒</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:57:29 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/turn-your-eyes-to-the-night-skies-this-week-to-see-a-near-total-lunar-eclipse-itll-temporarily-turn-the-moon-red-180989404/</guid></item><item><title>2200 年前的罗马沉船上的易碎涂层揭示了古代水手如何使船只保持漂浮</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/brittle-coating-on-2200-year-old-roman-shipwreck-revealing-how-ancient-soliders-kept-ships-afloat-180989394/</link><description>船上保存的松焦油和蜂蜡的痕迹揭示了几千年前造船厂用来保护船只免受深海侵蚀的艰苦技术</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:45:17 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/brittle-coating-on-2200-year-old-roman-shipwreck-revealing-how-ancient-soliders-kept-ships-afloat-180989394/</guid></item><item><title>查看年度野生动物摄影师奖中的 16 张令人惊叹的动物照片</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-16-stunning-animal-images-from-the-wildlife-photographer-of-the-year-awards-180989397/</link><description>这项著名的比赛现已进入第 62 个年头，在 10 月份宣布获奖者之前，先睹为快地公布了本次比赛的参赛作品</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:28:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-16-stunning-animal-images-from-the-wildlife-photographer-of-the-year-awards-180989397/</guid></item><item><title>这些中世纪手稿碎片被重新用作羊皮纸，无意中将它们保存了几个世纪</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-medieval-manuscript-fragments-were-reused-as-parchment-inadvertently-preserving-them-for-centuries-180989398/</link><description>最近在海峡群岛之一根西岛发现的这些书页包括圣经段落、诗歌、戏剧和其他文本。它们在 16 世纪和 17 世纪被重新用作书籍装订</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:20:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-medieval-manuscript-fragments-were-reused-as-parchment-inadvertently-preserving-them-for-centuries-180989398/</guid></item><item><title>迭戈·马拉多纳世界杯“上帝之手”进球所用的足球在拍卖会上以 335 万美元的价格售出</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/soccer-ball-used-for-diego-maradona-hand-of-god-world-cup-goal-sells-at-auction-180989392/</link><description>尽管它在足球历史上最著名的比赛之一中发挥了重要作用，但这件具有历史意义的体育纪念品的售价仍低于 1000 万美元的预售估价</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 17:02:31 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/soccer-ball-used-for-diego-maradona-hand-of-god-world-cup-goal-sells-at-auction-180989392/</guid></item><item><title>这种致命的贝类中毒没有解药。美国牛蛙中发现的一种蛋白质可能会改变这一现状</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-deadly-shellfish-poisoning-has-no-antidote-a-protein-found-in-american-bullfrogs-could-change-that-180989365/</link><description>一项针对小鼠的研究发现，一种名为亲蛤蚌毒素蛋白的蛋白质就像海绵一样，可以对抗藻华产生的致命毒素。这种有害物质在某些海鲜中积累，可能会导致一种危及生命的疾病，称为麻痹性贝类中毒</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 15:39:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-deadly-shellfish-poisoning-has-no-antidote-a-protein-found-in-american-bullfrogs-could-change-that-180989365/</guid></item><item><title>仍在建造中的新望远镜意外揭示了垂死恒星如何将物质带回太空</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-telescope-still-under-construction-accidentally-reveals-how-a-dying-star-returns-matter-to-space-180989349/</link><description>研究人员在校准位于智利的名为 MOTHRA 的仪器时捕获了前所未有的恒星回收过程图像，该仪器预计将于 2026 年底完成</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-telescope-still-under-construction-accidentally-reveals-how-a-dying-star-returns-matter-to-space-180989349/</guid></item><item><title>“饥饿石”在欧洲重新出现，随着河流跌至历史低点，数百年前的警告重新出现在人们的视野中</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/hunger-stones-resurface-europe-bringing-centuries-old-warnings-back-into-view-rivers-hit-historic-lows-180989387/</link><description>随着干旱使中欧大片河床裸露，过去几代人雕刻的记录低水位的标记再次出现</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 11:45:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/hunger-stones-resurface-europe-bringing-centuries-old-warnings-back-into-view-rivers-hit-historic-lows-180989387/</guid></item><item><title>在科罗拉多州首个肥胖土拨鼠周期间为最矮胖的高山啮齿动物投票</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/cast-your-vote-for-the-chunkiest-alpine-rodent-during-colorados-first-ever-fat-marmot-week-180989395/</link><description>首届比赛让八只黄腹土拨鼠正面交锋，同时揭示了它们季节性体重增加和高海拔生存背后的科学原理</description><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 19:33:40 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/cast-your-vote-for-the-chunkiest-alpine-rodent-during-colorados-first-ever-fat-marmot-week-180989395/</guid></item><item><title>马萨诸塞州一座新雕像纪念《白鲸》作者赫尔曼·梅尔维尔，他的捕鲸冒险就是从这里开始的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-statue-honors-moby-dick-author-herman-melville-in-the-massachusetts-city-where-his-whaling-adventures-began-180989388/</link><description>这件 7.5 英尺高的青铜艺术品矗立在历史悠久的新贝德福德市中心，这座 19 世纪的捕鲸港为作者在 1851 年创作著名小说提供了灵感</description><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 17:57:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-statue-honors-moby-dick-author-herman-melville-in-the-massachusetts-city-where-his-whaling-adventures-began-180989388/</guid></item><item><title>在苏格兰的一个神秘石结构内发现了一具人类骨骼。考古学家仍然不知道为什么它被埋在那里</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/human-skeleton-found-inside-mysterious-stone-structure-in-scotland-archaeologists-still-dont-know-why-it-was-buried-there-180989391/</link><description>这种不寻常的结构是用合适的石头和类似粘土的材料建造的，可能有助于保留液体，这种不寻常的结构让研究人员寻找解释</description><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 17:51:55 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/human-skeleton-found-inside-mysterious-stone-structure-in-scotland-archaeologists-still-dont-know-why-it-was-buried-there-180989391/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，这些小鼩鼱会长出更大的鼻子并缩小大脑以度过严冬</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-tiny-shrews-grow-bigger-snouts-and-shrink-their-brains-to-survive-harsh-winters-study-suggests-180989369/</link><description>科学家们早就知道，一些小型哺乳动物的大脑在寒冷的月份会缩小，并在春天重新生长。来自日本北海道的长爪鼩鼱似乎遵循这种模式，而令人惊讶的是它们的鼻子却相反</description><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:36:12 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-tiny-shrews-grow-bigger-snouts-and-shrink-their-brains-to-survive-harsh-winters-study-suggests-180989369/</guid></item><item><title>中国的这种岩画近2000年来一直保持鲜红色。如何？秘密成分可能是血</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-rock-art-in-china-has-remained-bright-red-for-nearly-2000-years-how-the-secret-ingredient-might-be-blood-180989389/</link><description>一项新的研究提供了关于洛越人如何在现在的中国南方创作岩画的线索。几个世纪以来，这些壁画都足够耐用，可以承受雨水、高温、风和湿度</description><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-rock-art-in-china-has-remained-bright-red-for-nearly-2000-years-how-the-secret-ingredient-might-be-blood-180989389/</guid></item><item><title>在法国，夏季的酷暑热浪正在对那些为克劳德·莫奈最受喜爱的画作提供灵感的花朵造成影响</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-france-brutal-summer-heat-waves-taking-toll-on-flowers-that-inspired-claude-monet-most-beloved-paintings-180989384/</link><description>今年夏天，法国正面临创纪录的 52 天热浪，艺术家家和花园里色彩缤纷的旱金莲受到了特别严重的打击。</description><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 20:06:03 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-france-brutal-summer-heat-waves-taking-toll-on-flowers-that-inspired-claude-monet-most-beloved-paintings-180989384/</guid></item><item><title>“独一无二”的水母博物馆安全地在玻璃后面展示令人惊叹的海荨麻，令游客惊叹不已</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/only-one-of-its-kind-jellyfish-museum-opens-in-florida-astounds-visitors-awe-inspiring-displays-nettles-safely-behind-glass-180989381/</link><description>该博物馆于春季开放，由两位逃离俄罗斯-乌克兰战争的水族馆专家创办</description><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 17:55:33 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/only-one-of-its-kind-jellyfish-museum-opens-in-florida-astounds-visitors-awe-inspiring-displays-nettles-safely-behind-glass-180989381/</guid></item><item><title>这条 15 英尺长的蟒蛇是已知的第一条接受电化学疗法治疗癌症的蛇。现在，她正式摆脱了这种疾病</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-15-foot-python-is-the-first-known-snake-to-receive-electrochemotherapy-for-cancer-now-shes-officially-free-of-the-disease-180989385/</link><description>这种开创性的治疗方法使传统化疗药物更容易渗透癌细胞。手术后，这只名叫朱迪·福斯特的爬行动物很快康复了</description><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 17:31:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-15-foot-python-is-the-first-known-snake-to-receive-electrochemotherapy-for-cancer-now-shes-officially-free-of-the-disease-180989385/</guid></item><item><title>自二战以来对公众关闭的伦敦自然历史博物馆的“隐藏”画廊再次向公众开放</title><link>http